{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6Qf466PeetLzaKKWvoAU8","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f","date":"2026-06-10T07:24:55+01:00","message":"(fix) De-duplicate repeated lab results in the test results viewer (#3345)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Tests results: dedupe lab results by conceptUuid to stop duplicate rows\n\nProblem\nOn the patient-chart lab results viewer, a single lab result is rendered\nmultiple times — once per order placed for that test. A NEW order plus its\nauto-generated DISCONTINUE order made the same result show twice; two orders,\nfour times, and so on.\n\nRoot cause\nThe /obstree backend returns the same orderable-test concept under several\nbranches of the orderable-tests tree (effectively one branch per order), each\nbranch carrying the same single observation. In filter-context's tableData\nbuilder the de-duplication key is based on test.flatName, which differs per\nbranch, so the identical observation is not collapsed and renders once per\nbranch.\n\nFix\nKey the de-duplication on the observation's conceptUuid instead of flatName.\nThe same observation (same concept + datetime + value) reached via different\nbranches now collapses to a single row, while genuinely different tests stay\nseparate. One-line change, no new dependencies, no new i18n keys.\n\n* (fix) Scope lab results dedupe to the rendered panel, not just conceptUuid\n\nKeying de-duplication on conceptUuid alone collapsed the same observation\nacross different rendered panels. A concept mounted under two roots (e.g.\nPlatelets under both Hematology and Bloodwork) was deduped to a single row,\ndropping the tree view from 3 tables to 2 and Platelets from 2 rows to 1.\n\nScope the dedupe key to the panel group key derived from flatName, so the\nsame concept that legitimately appears under different panels stays as\nseparate rows while true duplicates within one panel still collapse. Extract\nthe group-key derivation into a shared helper used by both the dedupe and the\ngrouping step so the two scopes stay aligned.\n\nAdd regression tests covering both directions: collapse within one panel and\nkeep across two panels.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"cerveaubleu64","authorEmail":"50305875+cerveaubleu64@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d7bdf92218d575a4f288da9151009a679b1c29d6","date":"2025-12-01T10:26:17+03:00","message":"(test) Add comprehensive tests for the results viewer (#2877)","refs":"","body":"* (test) Add comprehensive tests for the results viewer\n\nAdds 79 new tests covering filter state management, context providers,\nUI interactions, and data transformation logic. Refactor trendline\ncomponent with proper TypeScript types, memoization, and code quality\nimprovements.\n\nTests added:\n- filter-reducer.test.ts (21 tests)\n- filter-context.test.tsx (18 tests)\n- filter-set.test.tsx (17 tests)\n- useObstreeData.test.ts (15 tests)\n- tree-view.test.tsx (8 tests)\n\nImprovements:\n- Add TypeScript interfaces for trendline component props\n- Memoize data transformations for performance\n- Fix variable shadowing and remove dead code\n- Fix filter context useEffect dependencies\n- Optimize filter reducer state copying\n\nAll tests passing, linting and type checks clean.\n\n* Fix e2e test","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"dceb5439ca5640dad278a8442920ba310b6be5fa","date":"2025-11-11T22:29:17+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5189: Use criteria-based reference ranges from obstree response (#2840)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-5189: Use criteria-based reference ranges from obstree response\n\nThe REST web services module's obstree resource now includes:\n- Interpretation values at the observation level\n- Reference ranges at both node-level (concept defaults) and observation-level (criteria-based/\npatient-specific)\n\nCurrently, the patient chart only uses concept-level reference ranges. We need to migrate\nto prioritize criteria-based (observation-level) reference ranges, which are more accurate\nas they can be patient-specific, age-specific, or gender-specific. This is particularly\nimportant because observations are point-in-time values so, e.g., the reference range\nthat applies to an observation depends on the patients age at the time of the observation.\nThat is, the reference range for a value measured when a patient was 9 should not be\ndifferent because the patient is currently 13.\n\nChanges:\n- Update type definitions to include all reference range fields (hiAbsolute, hiCritical,\nlowAbsolute, lowCritical, lowNormal, hiNormal)\n- Implement priority logic: observation-level ranges (criteria-based) > node-level ranges\n(concept defaults) > \"--\"\n- Update interpretation calculation to use observation-level ranges when available\n- Update display logic across all UI components:\n  * Timeline view: Show most recent observation's range per row\n  * Individual results table: Show each observation's range\n  * Trendline: Use node-level range (aggregate view)\n  * Lab Set Panel: Show observation-level ranges when available\n- Extract reusable helper functions for range selection and formatting\n- Add comprehensive test coverage for new functionality\n- Fix type safety issues and improve code quality\n\n* Fixup","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5b176703509e49046e47be1a673687a360e0bed1","date":"2025-08-26T21:12:28+03:00","message":"(feat) Improve test results filtering and timeline display (#2701)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Improve test results filtering and timeline display\n\nThis PR makes the following improvements to the tests results viewer:\n\n- Refactors the filter reducer with improved action types and better tree structure handling\n- Replaces complex timeline scrolling with intersection observer navigation\n- Add filtered results count tracking alongside the total results count\n- Improved TypeScript safety and reduce prop drilling\n- Enhance responsive design and accordion styling\n- Optimize performance through better memoization and data structures\n- Fix parent/child checkbox relationships and indeterminate states\n\n* Review feedback: optimize data handling and sorting operations\n\n- Move data trimming to source (useObstreeData) for better performance\n- Remove redundant trimming in filter-context consumption\n- Improve date sorting efficiency with canonical approach","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"940f79820e6cf276d00489c013899a9b0c575569","date":"2025-04-30T08:17:30-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-4661: Test Results: Viewer drops imaging observations in tablet mode from Individual Tests view (#2405)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Brandon Istenes","authorEmail":"bistenes@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":5}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0cd011e-3d82-42c5-8e1a-effe14bad069","uuid":"29a58a21-61d8-4829-b923-efd7cd38039f","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:42:09.097Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f","date":"2026-06-10T07:24:55+01:00","message":"(fix) De-duplicate repeated lab results in the test results viewer (#3345)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Tests results: dedupe lab results by conceptUuid to stop duplicate rows\n\nProblem\nOn the patient-chart lab results viewer, a single lab result is rendered\nmultiple times — once per order placed for that test. A NEW order plus its\nauto-generated DISCONTINUE order made the same result show twice; two orders,\nfour times, and so on.\n\nRoot cause\nThe /obstree backend returns the same orderable-test concept under several\nbranches of the orderable-tests tree (effectively one branch per order), each\nbranch carrying the same single observation. In filter-context's tableData\nbuilder the de-duplication key is based on test.flatName, which differs per\nbranch, so the identical observation is not collapsed and renders once per\nbranch.\n\nFix\nKey the de-duplication on the observation's conceptUuid instead of flatName.\nThe same observation (same concept + datetime + value) reached via different\nbranches now collapses to a single row, while genuinely different tests stay\nseparate. One-line change, no new dependencies, no new i18n keys.\n\n* (fix) Scope lab results dedupe to the rendered panel, not just conceptUuid\n\nKeying de-duplication on conceptUuid alone collapsed the same observation\nacross different rendered panels. A concept mounted under two roots (e.g.\nPlatelets under both Hematology and Bloodwork) was deduped to a single row,\ndropping the tree view from 3 tables to 2 and Platelets from 2 rows to 1.\n\nScope the dedupe key to the panel group key derived from flatName, so the\nsame concept that legitimately appears under different panels stays as\nseparate rows while true duplicates within one panel still collapse. Extract\nthe group-key derivation into a shared helper used by both the dedupe and the\ngrouping step so the two scopes stay aligned.\n\nAdd regression tests covering both directions: collapse within one panel and\nkeep across two panels.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"cerveaubleu64","authorEmail":"50305875+cerveaubleu64@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d7bdf92218d575a4f288da9151009a679b1c29d6","date":"2025-12-01T10:26:17+03:00","message":"(test) Add comprehensive tests for the results viewer (#2877)","refs":"","body":"* (test) Add comprehensive tests for the results viewer\n\nAdds 79 new tests covering filter state management, context providers,\nUI interactions, and data transformation logic. Refactor trendline\ncomponent with proper TypeScript types, memoization, and code quality\nimprovements.\n\nTests added:\n- filter-reducer.test.ts (21 tests)\n- filter-context.test.tsx (18 tests)\n- filter-set.test.tsx (17 tests)\n- useObstreeData.test.