(fix) De-duplicate repeated lab results in the test results viewer (#3345)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Tests results: dedupe lab results by conceptUuid to stop duplicate rows\n\nProblem\nOn the patient-chart lab results viewer, a single lab result is rendered\nmultiple times — once per order placed for that test. A NEW order plus its\nauto-generated DISCONTINUE order made the same result show twice; two orders,\nfour times, and so on.\n\nRoot cause\nThe /obstree backend returns the same orderable-test concept under several\nbranches of the orderable-tests tree (effectively one branch per order), each\nbranch carrying the same single observation. In filter-context's tableData\nbuilder the de-duplication key is based on test.flatName, which differs per\nbranch, so the identical observation is not collapsed and renders once per\nbranch.\n\nFix\nKey the de-duplication on the observation's conceptUuid instead of flatName.\nThe same observation (same concept + datetime + value) reached via different\nbranches now collapses to a single row, while genuinely different tests stay\nseparate. One-line change, no new dependencies, no new i18n keys.\n\n* (fix) Scope lab results dedupe to the rendered panel, not just conceptUuid\n\nKeying de-duplication on conceptUuid alone collapsed the same observation\nacross different rendered panels. A concept mounted under two roots (e.g.\nPlatelets under both Hematology and Bloodwork) was deduped to a single row,\ndropping the tree view from 3 tables to 2 and Platelets from 2 rows to 1.\n\nScope the dedupe key to the panel group key derived from flatName, so the\nsame concept that legitimately appears under different panels stays as\nseparate rows while true duplicates within one panel still collapse. Extract\nthe group-key derivation into a shared helper used by both the dedupe and the\ngrouping step so the two scopes stay aligned.\n\nAdd regression tests covering both directions: collapse within one panel and\nkeep across two panels.\n\n\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>","authorName":"cerveaubleu64","authorEmail":"50305875+cerveaubleu64@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"bda2ce4aac69061ef4db6b45c88455f8cbd30e4c","date":"2026-05-13T19:56:26+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#3301)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"2d2a1bc1ab82e9ca3887fef2ac829c24a239cd99","date":"2026-04-16T23:50:29+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-5610: Add result date column to the lab order results table (#3225)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Laurent Ouma","authorEmail":"98098891+Omoshlawi@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"303e3a54bab29cc333630e8540f3db4481584147","date":"2026-04-15T21:06:05+03:00","message":"(fix) Fix tablet results viewer overlay issues (#3234)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"98e9eed004265810e4d86f3d6de873161307ba65","date":"2026-04-10T21:58:34+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5599: Use clean, lowercase, hyphenated URL paths for dashboard slugs (#3217)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a22a141d1fe85254ee72df26a356ed80dca6dd2d","date":"2026-04-02T04:23:14+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5436: Align test result columns in the Visits Tests tab (#3033)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Raj Prakash","authorEmail":"rjnt452@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f3cd34fbb63f26da653417dfaebfd4ca622e35e9","date":"2026-04-01T17:53:11+03:00","message":"(fix) Improve test results table styling and fix phantom column in timeline grid (#3194)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ecc67949fd3eb16588489ff6d7a81d5151d4238e","date":"2026-03-17T13:37:20+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5501: Replace duplicate ErrorState component with re-export from framework (#3115)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Soham Dhande","authorEmail":"sohamdhande1562007@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f16c75